WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.870
- But basically you think
you require money to be rich?

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.970
- Well you can also be rich in love.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.940
I'm feel like I'm already
rich in happiness.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.838
- Good.
- Because I have nice friends,

00:00:11.838 --> 00:00:16.050
I have a nice family, and
I have a pretty nice life.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:17.550
I'm actually pretty spoiled.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.870
- Don't tell your mother
and father, right? (laughs)

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.870
(suspenseful music)

00:00:32.236 --> 00:00:36.090
- [Interviewer] I am afraid of death.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:37.953
Those who agree, please step forward.

00:00:39.212 --> 00:00:41.795
(kids giggles)

00:00:43.428 --> 00:00:44.940
- Oh okay.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.398
I wanna sit in the middle.

00:00:46.398 --> 00:00:48.033
- I'm in the middle.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.080
- Like I feel like life is really short

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.780
and you have so much to
achieve in that period

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.040
and in that short period

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.630
you need to show the world your purpose.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:01.740
- Yeah, it's like I actually
had a close death experience

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.530
not that long ago and that was scary.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.510
So I'm gonna say it is even scarier

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:07.950
to actually have it happen!

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:10.731
- Well, death is probably
gonna be scary for me,

00:01:10.731 --> 00:01:12.453
because I'm a crybaby.

00:01:13.554 --> 00:01:15.960
I can barely handle height.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:19.620
If you wanted me to like
be on a rollercoaster,

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.260
I will be crying even before it started.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.530
- Yeah, but like the thing is
that if you don't take risks,

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.870
how will your life journey be rewarding?

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:29.850
Like if you guys are afraid of heights,

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:31.050
what if you try to overcome it?

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:34.020
And what if that makes
your life more memorable?

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.570
- I try to, but I kind of did enjoy it,

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.331
but at the same time it
felt like I'm about to die.

00:01:39.331 --> 00:01:40.290
(cowbell hits)

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:43.193
- [Interviewer] Now can I have
the disagree or step forward?

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.443
- Hello, disagreers.

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:54.030
- Death is part of living.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:58.061
It happens to everybody, to
some people sooner than others,

00:01:58.061 --> 00:02:01.488
but the important thing is
to try and live your life

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:04.562
how you think you want to live it.

00:02:04.562 --> 00:02:05.550
- I don't know how I want to live it.

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:10.230
- It's not an easy thing when
you lose someone you love.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.300
You learn to live without them

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.910
and hopefully you've gained something

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:19.140
from your relationship with those people.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:23.790
- I agree with you, it
just, and I honestly thought

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:24.855
that I was ready for death until,

00:02:24.855 --> 00:02:29.820
if I'm like bleeding, I'm
already like scared and crying

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.470
and I'm already thinking that I'm dying

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.006
if I'm already bleeding.

00:02:33.006 --> 00:02:35.968
- But death is just a part of life.

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:39.422
I equate death sometimes with a tree.

00:02:39.422 --> 00:02:42.540
What is happening to the trees now

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.710
with their leaves?

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:44.543
- They're falling.

00:02:44.543 --> 00:02:45.660
- They're falling.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:46.530
That's right.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:48.510
They're getting ready for new leaves

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.640
to come in the springtime

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.394
and it's just a natural part of life.

00:02:52.394 --> 00:02:53.880
- Yes.
- Okay.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.880
- Now that I'm getting
to my twilight years,

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:01.512
I am wondering what is going
to happen after I pass away.

00:03:01.512 --> 00:03:05.430
And that is the thing that I think about

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.764
more than anything else.

00:03:06.764 --> 00:03:07.597
(cowbell hits)

00:03:07.597 --> 00:03:09.733
I'm not a believer of God,

00:03:09.733 --> 00:03:13.049
and I am always just
wondering what is the purpose

00:03:13.049 --> 00:03:18.049
of being born and what is
going to be the hereafter?

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.250
That is something of course no one

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:22.740
will be able to give
you an answer on that.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:25.500
But I do believe in reincarnation.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:29.760
I feel that I'm coming back
to earth as maybe a newborn

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.568
or maybe as an animal
or something like that.

00:03:32.568 --> 00:03:33.480
(cowbell hits)

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.760
- In our religion we have
something called karma.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.333
So it's your good deeds come back to you

00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:42.702
and your bad deeds in the
afterlife come back to affect you,

00:03:42.702 --> 00:03:46.380
and that's why I feel
like the period you have

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:48.468
from like being a child growing up,

00:03:48.468 --> 00:03:52.170
you know, just progressing
through life, it's so important.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:55.200
But still like that thought
lingers in the back of my mind.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.990
Is there something that
will come to affect me?

00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:02.550
- Well, you know, my
son-in-love father died,

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.689
and I flew back to Oklahoma
City for his funeral

00:04:05.689 --> 00:04:10.689
and I did not see one wet
eye in that funeral service.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:17.220
Everybody was laughing, joking around,

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:21.390
because that's the way that Pawpaw lived.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:22.987
And I left their thinking,

00:04:22.987 --> 00:04:25.590
"I don't want people crying over me.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:30.270
I want them to be happy for
me and happy for themselves."

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:34.440
- And if you go to see,
let's say, a gravestone

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.370
and there's a dash between 1900 and 1970,

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:41.760
the most important thing is that dash.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.795
- What happened during that dash?

00:04:43.795 --> 00:04:44.749
- Yes.

00:04:44.749 --> 00:04:46.245
- The time that you lived

00:04:46.245 --> 00:04:49.220
and what you were able to accomplish,

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:53.580
and what kind of a legacy
did you leave to your family

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.888
and your heirs is very,
very important to me.

00:04:56.888 --> 00:04:58.410
(wind whooshes)

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:01.680
- [Interviewer] I have been in love.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:02.513
- Okay.

00:05:02.513 --> 00:05:04.400
- [Interviewer] Those
who agree, step forward.

00:05:06.202 --> 00:05:07.408
- Opposite this time!

00:05:07.408 --> 00:05:08.673
It's opposite this time!

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:11.600
- Unless you're counting family members.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:13.900
- Actually, yeah.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:19.180
- I suppose neither
one of you are married.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:20.140
(group laughs)

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:21.630
- No!

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:23.550
It's love in a different way.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.670
Love is, it's such a interesting force.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:27.720
It brings people together.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:30.000
It separates people but like still, yeah,

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.567
of course I have close ones
and I do dearly love them.

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:36.360
- But love can also be that dagger

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.793
in your heart.
- Yeah.

00:05:37.793 --> 00:05:39.670
Yeah, you're totally right.

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:44.155
- Well for me, yes, love
can be hard because for me,

00:05:44.155 --> 00:05:46.680
loved ones, we usually fight more

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:48.630
than I fight with a normal person,

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:51.259
but for me that just shows
that you really love them.

00:05:51.259 --> 00:05:54.210
Like I love my family because
they're really nice to me

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:55.740
and they really care for me.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:57.090
- That's wonderful.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:00.708
But what if they did not treat you nicely?

00:06:00.708 --> 00:06:02.519
- Well, they're still my family.

00:06:02.519 --> 00:06:04.276
I still gotta love 'em.
- And you still love them.

00:06:04.276 --> 00:06:05.492
That's right.

00:06:05.492 --> 00:06:07.230
- I am very fortunate.

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:11.040
I've been married to this
lovely woman for 63 years.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:11.873
- Wow!

00:06:11.873 --> 00:06:13.065
- Oh my god!

00:06:13.065 --> 00:06:16.380
- So that is virtually a lifetime.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:20.030
We have three daughters,
seven grandchildren,

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:23.129
and three great-grandchildren.

00:06:23.129 --> 00:06:25.177
- Somebody asked me,

00:06:25.177 --> 00:06:30.177
"how is it that you managed
to be married for 63 years?"

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.879
And I answered, "love
is a different story."

00:06:34.879 --> 00:06:38.460
Love is a person who cares about you,

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.350
you care about that person.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:41.640
If you're married a long time,

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:44.088
you experience a lot of things

00:06:44.088 --> 00:06:47.910
and some of 'em are very difficult,

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:51.043
and a lot of them are really wonderful.

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:55.041
So I always told our children,

00:06:55.041 --> 00:07:00.041
"you have to make time
for all the good times."

00:07:01.951 --> 00:07:02.965
(cowbell hits)

00:07:02.965 --> 00:07:07.965
- I love my family, my parents,
my pets and everything,

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:10.083
but when people say like in love

00:07:10.083 --> 00:07:12.450
I've like never had like
a crush or anything.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.130
I've never had like a
boyfriend or girlfriend.

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:15.750
No, none of that, no.

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:18.540
I feel glad that I'm not in love yet

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:21.060
because I don't at all feel ready.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:23.700
I wanna be those people
who don't have a crush,

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:26.250
and nobody has a crush on
them, because that's weird!

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:30.180
Like that makes me, that like
probably makes people think

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:33.180
that I'm cool and then it
makes them have a crush on me

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.830
and then they'll get a crush on me

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:36.630
and then I'll have like an army

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:38.190
of 20 boys following me around.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:39.750
I'm like, "ah!"

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:42.780
- Do you think that in the future

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:45.015
the love that your family gives you

00:07:45.015 --> 00:07:49.260
is equal to that of a love
that a partner would give you?

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:51.930
Like these guys definitely
love each other so much

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.210
and I think the love of your guys' family,

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:56.370
plus your guys' connection with each other

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:58.980
were the reasons you guys got
through hard times together.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:01.080
- I mean it could be true

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.692
that they love me as much as my family,

00:08:03.692 --> 00:08:06.630
like in six years from now

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:09.150
when I actually started
dating or something.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:11.399
The love and the things
your family teaches you

00:08:11.399 --> 00:08:14.011
are really like gonna
stay with you forever

00:08:14.011 --> 00:08:16.843
even though a lover might not.

00:08:16.843 --> 00:08:18.240
(air whooshes)

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:21.213
- [Interviewer] People are mostly good.

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:36.150
- I think that deep within everybody,

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:40.508
there is good inside them,
except it's with some people

00:08:40.508 --> 00:08:44.250
they haven't found themselves yet in life

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:47.122
to be able to show their goodness.

00:08:47.122 --> 00:08:52.122
- I would like to think
that everyone is good.

00:08:52.578 --> 00:08:55.770
But when I look at the news.

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:56.603
- Ooh.

00:08:56.603 --> 00:09:00.525
- For example, a family
completely annihilated

00:09:00.525 --> 00:09:03.510
just a few days ago.

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:06.720
Where was the goodness in that man

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:09.480
who murdered these people?

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.379
- So addressing that.

00:09:11.379 --> 00:09:16.140
You guys have all probably
faced bullying, right?

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:17.070
- Oh, yes.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:21.780
- So the person who
bullies another person,

00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:25.200
they have something that's affecting them,

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:27.364
whether it be like their personal issues,

00:09:27.364 --> 00:09:29.189
issues with their family,

00:09:29.189 --> 00:09:32.010
and that kind of, in the future,

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:35.400
makes them resort to
means that aren't good.

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:36.900
And sometimes it's not their fault.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:39.060
It could be of their mental health issues,

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:40.920
it could be because of the background,

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:43.500
like if they've been abused
when they were young.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:45.810
Just because you do bad
things in the future,

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:48.600
you annihilated, you commit crimes.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:50.490
I don't think that means
that you're a bad person.

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:53.790
I just think that means you're not showing

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:55.980
the good side of you,
you're showing the bad side.

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:57.270
- A lot of it could be

00:09:57.270 --> 00:09:59.730
a mental illness too.
- Yes.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:03.384
- And there are a lot of people
who have that mental illness

00:10:03.384 --> 00:10:06.870
and therefore can't show their good side.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.515
- There are a lot of good people,

00:10:08.515 --> 00:10:10.320
and you may be right,

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:14.499
maybe everybody has
the ability to be good,

00:10:14.499 --> 00:10:16.980
but some people don't exercise it.

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:21.980
And again, there are people who, I think,

00:10:22.307 --> 00:10:27.030
somebody kills someone,
of course they're sick.

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:29.190
That's gotta be something mentally wrong

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.294
that you're going to kill somebody.

00:10:30.294 --> 00:10:31.530
(air whooshes)

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:35.100
45 years ago, we were followed home,

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:38.680
and when we got home, we
were held up with a gun

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:43.080
and he said he was going to kill me.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:48.080
So he took my ring and
took my husband's car keys.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.610
And right now, it's worse.

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:52.710
The children are not safe.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:54.960
Our children are our future.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:58.834
If they're not safe, who is?

00:10:58.834 --> 00:11:00.810
And it's not getting better.

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:03.840
They're not, it's happening more and more.

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:05.220
It's horrible.

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:07.653
So no, I don't think it's safe now.

00:11:08.552 --> 00:11:09.798
(cowbell dings)

00:11:09.798 --> 00:11:12.802
- Well, for me, I kind of disagree,

00:11:12.802 --> 00:11:15.802
because yes, there is good in people,

00:11:15.802 --> 00:11:20.649
but people can be very bad
whether we like it or not.

00:11:20.649 --> 00:11:23.820
Because for me, I do have a bad side.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:27.210
It might be just because I
get like angry really easily,

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:30.440
but I can think mean thoughts too,

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:33.090
but I try not to say it.

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:35.991
I get mad easily whether
you believe it or not.

00:11:35.991 --> 00:11:39.510
I will literally scream at you.

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:41.610
One time when my friend was called a brat,

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:43.860
I was about to go full
crazy on that person,

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:46.470
but instead I tried to be nice.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:48.320
But I couldn't help it, I was like...

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:53.370
- I do think there is mostly
good people in the world.

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:55.083
Actually everybody in the world is good,

00:11:55.083 --> 00:11:59.430
but the bad people just
wanna show their bad side.

00:11:59.430 --> 00:12:02.343
So then they're just the bad people

00:12:02.343 --> 00:12:05.490
that we think about when
we think bad people,

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:09.210
because they did things
they weren't supposed to

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:11.801
and they did it 'cause they wanted to.

00:12:11.801 --> 00:12:16.801
- I was always taught the golden rule.

00:12:17.186 --> 00:12:18.930
- Treat others-
- Treat others the way

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:19.950
you way you wanna be treated.

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:21.450
- That's right.

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:24.450
I would like to be treated kindly,

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:26.730
and I would hope that people

00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:28.978
are teaching their children that.

00:12:28.978 --> 00:12:30.360
(air whooshes)

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:33.363
- [Interviewer] I would love to be rich.

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:48.073
- Well, for me, I'd love to be rich,

00:12:48.073 --> 00:12:51.810
because let's say I have
like a million dollars.

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:54.060
I can invest in stocks first,

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:57.510
and then I can like start a business,

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:59.400
and then I can make more money.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:01.110
And then the more money that I get,

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:03.420
I can also help other people.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:05.705
Like I can help poor people,
I can donate to charities,

00:13:05.705 --> 00:13:09.720
and I can also help out
myself and other people.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:13.500
- But basically you think
you require money to be rich.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:16.140
- Well, you can also be rich in love with-

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:19.500
- But you can be rich in other
things and what you have.

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:21.540
- Like a great personality too.

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:22.373
- Yes.

00:13:22.373 --> 00:13:23.850
I think I am rich,

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:27.450
because I'm blessed
with a wonderful family.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.520
- I think that a lot
of times what happens,

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:32.025
people think of accumulating wealth,

00:13:32.025 --> 00:13:34.876
which is a sign of happiness.

00:13:34.876 --> 00:13:38.190
And happiness to me is, there's one word.

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:39.811
It's contentment.

00:13:39.811 --> 00:13:43.980
If you are content with your
life and what you're doing,

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:48.900
I think you're then very, very
happy and very, very rich.

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:51.870
- I'm feel like I'm
already rich in happiness.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:52.703
